From: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa2-lite: emit a real unconditional catch-all

The terminal IPv4/IPv6 modem rules arrive in either byte-lane representation:
mask/value 0xf0/0x40 (0x60 for IPv6), or 0xf0000000/0x40000000
(0x60000000).  The previous workaround recognized only the former while the
decoded rule used the latter, then serialized to the former.  A live dump of
the AP table consequently still contained OFFSET_MEQ32_0 and no uplink packet
matched it.

Recognize both wire representations.  Make the family-terminal rule truly
unconditional by clearing the equation bitmap and count, rather than retaining
an OFFSET_MEQ32 operation with a zero mask.  The separate v4/v6 hardware table
already supplies the family selection.

Signed-off-by: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c b/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
index c3c8d61..20f4900 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
@@ -502,11 +502,14 @@ static int ipa_filter_build(struct ipa *ipa,
 		if (rules[i].filter_rule.rule_eq_bitmap == BIT(2) &&
 		    rules[i].filter_rule.num_offset_meq_32 == 1 &&
 		    rules[i].filter_rule.offset_meq_32[0].offset == 0 &&
-		    rules[i].filter_rule.offset_meq_32[0].mask == 0xf0 &&
-		    (rules[i].filter_rule.offset_meq_32[0].value == 0x40 ||
-		     rules[i].filter_rule.offset_meq_32[0].value == 0x60)) {
+		    ((rules[i].filter_rule.offset_meq_32[0].mask == 0xf0 &&
+		      (rules[i].filter_rule.offset_meq_32[0].value == 0x40 ||
+		       rules[i].filter_rule.offset_meq_32[0].value == 0x60)) ||
+		     (rules[i].filter_rule.offset_meq_32[0].mask == 0xf0000000 &&
+		      (rules[i].filter_rule.offset_meq_32[0].value == 0x40000000 ||
+		       rules[i].filter_rule.offset_meq_32[0].value == 0x60000000)))) {
 			family_catchall = rules[i];
-			family_catchall.filter_rule.offset_meq_32[0].mask = 0;
-			family_catchall.filter_rule.offset_meq_32[0].value = 0;
+			family_catchall.filter_rule.rule_eq_bitmap = 0;
+			family_catchall.filter_rule.num_offset_meq_32 = 0;
 			emit_rule = &family_catchall;
 		}
